  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "SDK Version:\nAll versions of Worlds SDK3 as of Nov 2022\nDescription of the bug:\nWhen many (hundreds) GameObjects with the same name are direct children of the same parent GameObject, the SDK's Build tab freezes for a long period of time when opened or focused. This can be especially affecting when dealing with foliage props.\nSteps to reproduce:\nCreate hundreds or thousands of GameObjects with the same name, as children under the same parent GameObject, then click on the Builder tab/page of the SDK.\nHypothesis:\nI think that the cause is the SDK's process of comparing the GameObjects' names against each other in order to provide the attached networking warning. (The length of the name also affects the duration, and it increases exponentially with the number of objects.)\nNote:\nMany artists use GameObjects for foliage, in conjunction with foliage painting tools - these all place the foliage objects with the same name, under the same parent object in the hierarchy. This issue is currently affecting our iteration time, freezing the editor for >1min after clicking on the SDK panel, as we recently created a foliage painter tool for our worlds.",
